      "title": "ArchiMate models — every view, element and relationship a node",
      "description": "ArchiMate models as knowledge-graph content: how an instance declares the Archi models it holds, what the `archimate` subgraph gives every model, view, element and relationship (an IRI, a thin page, and every view drawn as SVG from the model's own diagram, and its metamodel derived and checked), how to version the models, how to wire them into a folio's staging build and navbar, how to count and lower the crossed lines in a view before committing it, why every view carries a plain-language key, why names are the source's own terms linked to their SKOS concepts, and why no Java, no Archi CLI and no Archi HTML report is ever part of the pipeline. Read before adding, authoring, publishing or rendering an `.archimate` file, before citing an ArchiMate element from prose, and before reaching for Archi's own tooling in CI.",
